    {
      "id": "no_timer_check_path",
      "question": "Without no_timer_check, does check_timer go through IOAPIC pin 2 (ISO 0->2), and is that path implemented?",
      "decision": "Do not set no_timer_check. check_timer runs only if global_clock_event != NULL (PIT or HPET). HPET is absent, so PIT is global_clock_event unless apic_needs_pit() is false (needs ARAT plus a known LAPIC period, not the case unless CPUID 0x15/ARAT are exposed). pin1 comes from the ISO (IRQ0->GSI2), pin2 is -1 (no ExtINT). Success needs jiffies > t1+4, i.e. at least 5 PIT ticks at HZ=1000. delay_with_tsc gives up after 40000000000/HZ = 40M TSC cycles (io_apic.c:1484-1491), so TSC frequency relative to the board clock must not exceed about 8 GHz (40M cycles / 5 ms), otherwise the failure branch is taken.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c",
          "line": 2060,
          "excerpt_short": "if (!global_clock_event) return;"
        },
        {
          "file": "arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c",
          "line": 2087,
          "excerpt_short": "..TIMER: vector=0x%02X apic1=%d pin1=%d apic2=%d pin2=%d"
        },
        {
          "file": "arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c",
          "line": 2124,
          "excerpt_short": "if (timer_irq_works()) { ... goto out; }"
        },
        {
          "file": "arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c",
          "line": 1523,
          "excerpt_short": "if (no_timer_check) return 1;"
        },
        {
          "file": "arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c",
          "line": 1543,
          "excerpt_short": "return time_after(jiffies, t1 + 4);"
        },
        {
          "file": "arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c",
          "line": 2188,
          "excerpt_short": "panic(\"IO-APIC + timer doesn't work!"
        },
        {
          "file": "arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c",
