    {
      "id": "aeoi_in_check_timer",
      "question": "Does check_timer write ICW4 with AEOI, and does that interfere when global_clock_event != NULL?",
      "decision": "check_timer calls init_8259A(1): master ICW4 = 0x03, slave ICW4 = 0x01 (so slave AEOI rejection is never hit). It does not interfere: LVT0 is masked and the pair has no INTR. BUT at HEAD cc70151 (committed code) the model rejects master ICW4 with AEOI; the S4-29a2 slice named in decision 9 does not exist in the plan or in the committed code at HEAD cc70151; the uncommitted S4-29a2 change in the working tree is out of scope of this audit and not used as a source. This is a blocker for S4-38.",
