      "id": "cmos_rtc_requirements",
      "question": "Which Linux code reads CMOS on the boot path, and does the selected config require an RTC to boot?",
      "decision": "The RTC is not required to boot (rtc_cmos is not probed: FADT NO_CMOS_RTC -> legacy.rtc=0, no PNP0B00 in the DSDT). One mandatory CMOS read remains: timekeeping_init -> mach_get_cmos_time -> mc146818_get_time(timeout 1000 ms) is unconditional. With reg A = 0xFF (UIP=1) it loops up to about 10000 iterations of udelay(100), about 1 s of virtual time, then logs 'Unable to read current time from RTC' and continues with time 0. No hang, no panic, provided RDTSC/udelay advance.",
